{"id":"b670899f-6122-4cbf-b90a-ce7832536941","object":"chat.completion","created":1784838935,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    import json\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core_dist = case['core_distance']\\n    distances = case['distances']\\n    n = len(nodes)\\n    # Validate core distances for all nodes\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        if node not in core_dist:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Missing core distance for node {node}\\\")\\n    # Build edge map: frozenset([a,b]) -> (a,b,dist)\\n    edge_map = {}\\n    for a, b, d in distances:\\n        key = frozenset([a, b])\\n        if key in edge_map:\\n            # duplicate edge, keep first? For safety, raise\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Duplicate edge between {a} and {b}\\\")\\n        edge_map[key] = (a, b, d)\\n    # Compute mutual reachability for each unique pair\\n    edges = []\\n    for (a, b, d) in edge_map.values():\\n        ca = core_dist[a]\\n        cb = core_dist[b]\\n        mr = max(ca, cb, d)\\n        # canonicalize endpoints for tie-breaking\\n        if a < b:\\n            left, right = a, b\\n        else:\\n            left, right = b, a\\n        edges.append((mr, left, right))\\n    # Sort by mr, then left, then right\\n    edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1], x[2]))\\n    # Union-Find\\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\\n            parent[rx] = ry\\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n        else:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    for mr, u, v in edges:\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            mst_edges.append({'node1': u, 'node2': v, 'mutual_reachability': mr})\\n            total_weight += mr\\n            if len(mst_edges) == n - 1:\\n                break\\n    if len(mst_edges) != n - 1:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Input graph is disconnected; cannot form MST\\\")\\n    return {'edges': mst_edges, 'total_weight': total_weight}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to produce a JSON object with a single key \"implementation\" containing Python source for solve(case). The task is to compute mutual-reachability MST given nodes, core_distances, and distances. The description: compute core distances (given), mutual-reachability weights, then deterministic MST via Kruskal. Must handle ties by sorting edges by mutual reachability, then endpoint IDs (lexicographically). Use union-find. Return edges list and total_weight. Reject disconnected inputs: if after processing all edges we don't have n-1 edges, raise ValueError. The case payload has nodes list, core_distance dict, distances list of triples (node1, node2, distance). We need to compute mutual reachability for each pair: max(core_left, core_right, distance). Then sort edges by (mutual_reachability, min_endpoint, max_endpoint) (since endpoints are undirected, canonicalize by sorting IDs). Then Kruskal. Return dict with \"edges\" (list of dicts: node1, node2, mutual_reachability) and \"total_weight\". Also need to validate that all nodes have core distances, distances cover all pairs? Not required, but we assume given distances are all unique pairs? The fixture shows 10 distances for 5 nodes, which is complete. But we should handle any set, but if not enough edges to form MST, raise ValueError. Also can't assume graph is complete; we must use only given distances. If graph disconnected, error. Implementation must be pure Python.\n\nWrite solve(case) that returns a dict. Use standard library. No external libs.\n\nEdge case: duplicate edges? Not given. But we only consider each pair once. Since distances list may not be sorted, we can build a dictionary keyed by frozenset of endpoints to ensure we process each undirected pair once. Then compute mutual reachability for each pair. Then sort edges. Union-find with path compression and union by rank.\n\nAlso ensure we don't mutate case. Use copy? Not needed if we don't modify.\n\nReturn total_weight as float, sum of mutual_reachability of selected edges.\n\nCheck for connectivity: after processing all edges, if selected edges < n-1, raise ValueError.\n\nAlso need to ensure that all nodes appear in core_distance dict. Validate.\n\nWrite code as string. Escape JSON.\n\nLet's produce the Python source."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1652,"completion_tokens":1151,"total_tokens":2803,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1536},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":495},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1536,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":116},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}